<title>ALGERIA: Algeria signs $31.7 mln gas deal with Agip.</title>
<headline>Algeria signs $31.7 mln gas deal with Agip.</headline>
<dateline>ALGIERS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's state oil and gas firm Sonatrach and Italian Eni's unit Agip on Tuesday signed a $31.7 million gas exploration contract in Algiers, state media said.</p>
<p>The &quot;production sharing&quot; deal spanned five years and would involve sinking five test wells in In-Amedjane region in the hunt for new humid gas deposits.</p>
<p>The research programme will also involve seismic research in the area which lies southeast of Hassi Messaoud, Algeria's main oil field in the Sahara desert, the official news agency APS said.</p>
</text>
